# Privacy Policy for "I Don't Care"

_Last updated: October 2025_

Thank you for using **I Don't Care** (“the App”).  
This Privacy Policy explains how your information is handled when you use this Android application.

---

## 1. Overview

**I Don't Care** is a privacy-first Android app developed by **Piscesbn**.  
The app helps you filter and automatically dismiss unwanted marketing notifications.  
It operates entirely on your device and does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data to external servers.

Your privacy is our top priority.

---

## 2. Information Collection and Use

The app does **not** collect or share any personal information.  
Specifically, the app:

- Does not collect, store, or transmit user data.  
- Does not require an internet connection.  
- Does not use analytics tools or tracking SDKs.  
- Does not display or serve ads.  

All filtering and logic happen locally on your device.

---

## 3. Notification Access Permission

The app requires **Notification Access** permission to function.  
This permission allows the app to read incoming notifications in order to filter and dismiss unwanted ones based on your custom keywords and app whitelist.

The app:
- Only uses this access to perform filtering operations.  
- Does **not** save, upload, or share the content of your notifications.  
- Processes notification data in real time and discards it immediately after filtering.

---

## 4. Data Security

Since the app does not collect or transmit any data, there is no risk of data leakage or unauthorized sharing.  
All preferences (such as keywords and whitelisted apps) are stored locally on your device using Android’s **Jetpack DataStore**.

---

## 5. Changes to This Policy

If this policy is ever updated (for example, to reflect new features or legal requirements), the new version will be published in the app’s GitHub repository and/or Google Play Store listing.

You are encouraged to review this page periodically for any changes.

